# (auto-translated)
#: ../hacks/config/quasicrystal.xml.h:14
msgid ""
"\n"
"A quasicrystal is a structure that is ordered but aperiodic.\n"
"\n"
"Two-dimensional quasicrystals can be generated by adding a set of\n"
"planes where x is the sine of y.  Different complex aperiodic plane\n"
"tilings are produced depending on the period, position, and rotation\n"
"of the component planes, and whether the rotation of the planes is\n"
"evenly distributed around the circle (the \"symmetry\" option, above)\n"
"or random.\n"
"\n"
"See also the \"RD-Bomb\", \"CWaves\" and \"Penrose\" screen savers.\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quasicrystal\n"
"\n"
"Written by Jamie Zawinski; 2013.\n"
"  "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Un quasi-cristal est une structure ordonnée mais apériodique.\n"
"\n"
"les carrelages sont réalisés en fonction de la période, de la position et de "
"la rotation\n"
"des plans composants, et si la rotation des plans est\n"
"Des quasi-cristaux bidimensionnels peuvent être générés en ajoutant un "
"ensemble de\n"
"uniformément réparti autour du cercle (l'option \"symétrie\", ci-dessus)\n"
"plans où x est le sinus de y.  ou aléatoire.Différents plans apériodiques "
"complexes\n"
"\n"
"Voir aussi les économiseurs d'écran \"RD-Bomb\", \"CWaves\" et \"Penrose\".\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quasicrystal\n"
"\n"
"Écrit par Jamie Zawinski; 2013.\n"
"  "

